# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Living Archive — vault ignore rules
#
# This repo IS an Obsidian vault. Obsidian writes machine-local state and
# plugin secrets into it as a side effect of normal use. Nothing below is
# something you authored — it is state, cache, or credentials.
#
# The rule of thumb: vault *settings* are portable and worth versioning;
# vault *state* and anything a plugin stores on your behalf are not.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plugin settings live in data.json, and that is where API keys land — Copilot,
# Text Generator, Smart Connections, remotely-save (S3/WebDAV creds), any plugin
# that talks to a paid service. Ignored by default; a plugin whose settings you
# genuinely want versioned can be force-added: git add -f .obsidian/plugins/x/data.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
credentials.json
*_token
*.token
.netrc

# ── Obsidian machine-local state ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Window layout and open-file history. Churns on every session and records
# which notes you had open — noise in a diff, and a small leak besides.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/graph.json
.obsidian/hotkeys.json.bak

# Obsidian's local trash: deleted notes still fully readable on disk.
.trash/
.obsidian/trash/

# ── Local AI / embedding caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# These hold a vectorized copy of every note in the vault — the whole corpus in
# another form, often several hundred MB. Rebuildable from the notes themselves.
.smart-env/
.smart-connections/
.obsidian/plugins/*/vectors/
.rag/
.rag_index/
rag_index/
*.faiss
*.ann
embeddings/
*.embeddings.json

# ── Sync conflicts and third-party sync scratch ──────────────────────────────
*.sync-conflict-*
*conflicted copy*
.obsidian/sync.json
.stfolder/
.stversions/

# ── Private writing (convention, opt-in) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Anything you want kept off the remote goes in one of these. Files already
# committed are unaffected — this governs what you add from here on.
_private/
99_Private/
*.private.md

# ── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
